-- An @nlg on its own line above a rule belongs to that rule, whatever comes
-- before it. Each of these rules has no GIVEN, so the annotation sits outside the
-- rule's own span, and used to be taken by the name before it: a section heading,
-- a name at the end of the rule above, or the type of a DECLARE.

§ `Own line`

§§ `First section`

@nlg the first constant
`first constant` MEANS 1

@nlg the second constant
`second constant` MEANS `first constant`

@nlg the third constant
`third constant` MEANS `second constant`

DECLARE `declared constant` IS A NUMBER
@nlg the declared constant
`declared constant` MEANS 4

-- A slot means the rule's input, not a rule or a record field of the same name.
DECLARE Message HAS
  role IS A STRING

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
day x MEANS x

GIVEN day  IS A NUMBER
      role IS A STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the day %day% for %role%
`slotted rule` day role MEANS day

GIVETH A NUMBER
`uses them` MEANS `slotted rule` 3 "the tenant" PLUS `third constant` PLUS `declared constant`
